{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/1191765-specialties-after-character-generation","id":1191765,"title":"Specialties after character generation","path":["Home","Onyx Path","Onyx Path Worlds","The Trinity Continuum"],"posts":[{"date":"2018-03-04T15:59:01-08:00","id":1191765,"title":"Specialties after character generation","content":"Is it too late to make it so that getting 3 in a skill, both before and after character generation, gives you a specialty? I assumed this was the case until one of my players, who's wary of chargen optimization traps, noticed it and started to make sure that all his skills were at 3 so he didn't start with a deficit of potential XP. The rest of Storypath has been good at avoiding this, without scaling XP costs or other traditional pitfalls, and Scion explicitly already works this way, so I was hoping it could be added here as well.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23646-goblinsociety","name":"GoblinSociety","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"19"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-03-05T05:19:38-08:00","id":1191896,"title":"","content":"I hadn't actually thought about that. I'd already noticed that you can gain 2XP from choosing a dot of Psi instead of an attribute dot, but making sure you hit all skills at 3 is a much more onerous one. Not a fan. <br /> <br /> Worth noting though that Scion actually works the same way as TC <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Scion Page 105</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">Specialties are only free during character creation.</div> </div> </div> </div>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2649-tarion","name":"Tarion","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"85"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-03-06T04:59:33-08:00","id":1192202,"title":"","content":"Oh, whoops. When I was scanning Scion to see if they did the same thing there, I saw &quot;However, once a character reaches three or more dots in a Skill they may choose a Specialty focus, writing it next to the Skill on their character sheet.&quot; and assumed that they meant that as a procedural part of hitting 3 in a skill, rather than as an option. Looks like I need to make this post on the Scion boards, too!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23646-goblinsociety","name":"GoblinSociety","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"19"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}